            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for a wedding procession, then the Marathi for a marquee."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: आहेर",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आहेर — āher — \"a wedding gift\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मामांनी नवरीला साडीचा आहेर दिला. māmānnī navrīlā sāḍīcā āher dilā. Uncle gave the bride a sari as a wedding gift."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आहेर (āher) करणे or देणे, to give the customary gift."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आहेर (āher) is a tadbhava: CDIAL lists Marathi āher, 'presents to a family celebrating a marriage', under Sanskrit abhihāra, 'a bringing near' (CDIAL 534)."
            }
          ]
        },
