              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सनई — sanaī — \"a shehnai\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "लग्नघरात सकाळपासून सनई वाजत होती. lagnagharāt sakāḷpāsūn sanaī vājat hotī. The shehnai had been playing in the wedding house since morning."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A reed pipe played at weddings and festivals."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सनई (sanaī) names the reed pipe of weddings. It is usually traced to Persian, to surnāy, 'a festive pipe', or to šahnāy, 'a royal pipe'; which one, and by what path, is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
